{"n": 210, "w": 1000, "h": 764, "img": "210.webp", "text": "12-112/5\n\nFAULTS\n900 fault memory: 8 fault lamp\n\nExplanation; Only applicable for US models.\nThis fault Is stored when shorts occur on fault lamp or lis power supply lead.\n\nTroubleshooting: as displayed on screen.\n\nFAULT 12\n900 fault memory: 12 throttle valve potentiometer\n\nExplanation: This fault |S stored when shorts or breaks occur on potentiometer\nor Its power supply leads.\n\nTroubleshooting: as displayed on screen, Test values - see component testing.\n\nFAULT 16\n900 fault memory: 16 camshaft sender\n\nExplanation: This fault Is stored when faulty signals from camshaft sender oc-\ncurt at speed of > 2500 rpm.\n\nTroubleshooting: as displayed on screen.\n\nFAULT 29\n900 fault memory: 29 Idle speed contro!\nExplanation: This fault Is stored when a short or break occurs in Icad to pin 29.\n\nTroubleshooting: as displayed on screen.\n\nFAULT 32\n900 fault memory: 32 fuel injectors - cyl. 2+ 4\n\nExplanation: see Fault 3.\n\nFAULT 36\n900 fault memory: 36 tank venting valve\n\nExplanation: This fault is stored when a short or break occurs on tank venting\nvalve or Its power supply lead.\n\nTroubleshooting: as displayed on screen. Test values - see component testing.\n\nFAULT 87\n900 fault memory: 37 oxygen sensor heating relay\n\nExplanation: Fault Is stored when a short or break on relay or power supply\nlead from DME control unit pin 37 Is recognized.\n\nTroubleshooting: as displayed on screen.\n\nFAULT 41\n900 fault memory: 41 air flow sensor\n\nExplanation: This fault Is stored when shorts or breaks occur on alr flow sen-\nsor or Its leads (power supply or signal lead).\n\nAlso recognition when Up/Uv value of LMM Is no longer In the normal operat-\ning range of 0.02 to 0.95.\n\nDME control unit then works with determined replacement values, load signal\ntL = 3.5 ms (partial load) and 6.0 ms (full load) and ignition timing = 20 crank-\nshaft degrees before TDC.\n\nTroubleshooting: as displayed on screen.\n\nTest alr flow sensor with status call 200. Up/Uv value shows the relation betw.\npotentiometer voltage (slider) and power supply voltage (5 V) In air flow sensor,\nSpecifications —- see component testing.\n\nFAULT 54\n\n900 fault memory: 54 control unit power supply\n\nExplanation: This fault Is stored when power supply exceeds 16 V. A drop\nbelow 9 V Is recognized 3 minutes after starting at the earliest.\n\nPossible Fault Causes:\n\n- Contact resistance on lead connections\n- Incorrect drive belt tightness\n\n= Voltage regulator or alternator faulty\n\nTroubleshooting: as displayed on screen.\n\nFAULT 70\n900 fault memory: 70 oxygen sensor\n\nExplanation: This fault is stored when a short or break occurs on oxygen sen-\nsor or Its leads, or when no oxygen senor !s Installed (cars prepared for cata-\nlytic converter). It requires an engine temperature of > 70° C (158° F) over a pe-\ntlod of 3 minutes and a load signal of 3.5 ms for 5 seconds.\n\nTroubleshooting: as displayed on screen.\nTest values for oxygen sensor — see component testing.", "words": [["12-112/5", 0.4514, 0.0318, 0.5542, 0.0557], ["FAULTS", 0.0324, 0.0862, 0.08, 0.0975], ["900", 0.0324, 0.1194, 0.0517, 0.1313], ["fault", 0.0562, 0.12, 0.079, 0.1313], ["memory:", 0.0831, 0.122, 0.1282, 0.134], ["8", 0.1322, 0.1194, 0.1378, 0.1313], ["fault", 0.1418, 0.1194, 0.1646, 0.1313], ["lamp", 0.1692, 0.12, 0.1945, 0.134], ["Explanation;", 0.0329, 0.1525, 0.1003, 0.1664], ["Only", 0.1044, 0.1525, 0.1277, 0.1671], ["applicable", 0.1312, 0.1532, 0.1854, 0.1671], ["for", 0.19, 0.1532, 0.2042, 0.1645], ["US", 0.2082, 0.1525, 0.2229, 0.1645], ["models.", 0.227, 0.1532, 0.2685, 0.1645], ["This", 0.0329, 0.1698, 0.0567, 0.1804], ["fault", 0.0608, 0.1698, 0.0841, 0.1804], ["Is", 0.0876, 0.1698, 0.0963, 0.181], ["stored", 0.1003, 0.1698, 0.1327, 0.181], ["when", 0.1368, 0.1698, 0.1651, 0.181], ["shorts", 0.1692, 0.1698, 0.2026, 0.181], ["occur", 0.2067, 0.1718, 0.2371, 0.181], ["on", 0.2406, 0.1718